      "writtenOn": "2015-03-05T16:56:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "still thinking about this. we now read this ADC from three places: charge manager when we log power info, charge ramp to know if vbus is sagging and here. this means we have at least 3 tasks i count that can call this. looking at adc_read_channel() this appears safe, it just uses a mutex which means we might delay at any one of these places.\n\nwould it be better to use a hook to regularly read this ADC and then have all three places just use last read value? i think we would need this to be a hook_tick because the ramping needs a very recent value for this ADC, hook_second could cause problems detecting vbus sag.\n\nany opinions? is it better to leave like this or move to a hook_tick? or any other ideas?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 814,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 814,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "84e18698f7f5957c441c10fe63628f57220b8379",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7220f282_41d03547",
        "filename": "board/samus_pd/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
